    "result_text": "`BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 255 tests, 0 failures/errors. The `Unexpected error` log line comes from a pre-existing error-handling test, not this path (the acceptance test asserts exactly 409 and passes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all owner duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey` = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`, rejecting with 409 only on a whole-key match.\n\n**New files**\n- `OwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 shared helper deriving `identityKey` (E.164-normalized telephone, trimmed/lower-cased email, verbatim householdId), used by both the check and the response mapper.\n- `RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 the one consolidated check; throws checked `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` only when a new owner's whole `identityKey` equals an existing owner's.\n- `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException.java` + `DuplicateOwnerIdentityExceptionHandler.java` + its escalation YAML \u2192 409 Conflict.\n\n**Rewiring** (`owners.POST.yml`)\n- Moved `assignHousehold` **before** the duplicate check, so any shared `householdId` is part of the key at check time.\n- Replaced the three separate reject steps (`RejectDuplicateOwnerTelephone`, `-Email`, `-Household`) with the single `rejectDuplicateIdentity`.\n\n**Response** (`Return 'identityKey'`)\n- Added a read-only `identityKey` to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`.\n- Mapped it in `OwnerMapper` via `OwnerIdentity.identityKey(owner)`.\n\n**Removed** the three old reject functions, their exceptions, handlers, and escalation YAMLs, and fixed the dangling javadoc link in `AssignOwnerHousehold`.\n\n**Behaviour change (as specified):** because telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have distinct `identityKey`s and are both allowed \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate. The provided acceptance test (`coreRejectsIdentityCollision`: two owners sharing a telephone, both with empty email and empty householdId \u2192 equal keys \u2192 409) passes.",
